{"at": "2026-11-26T02:15:10.611Z", "run": "20261126-0015-verify-debrid-3523", "unit": "u15", "op": "set", "rid": "debrid/debridr", "path": "$.notes", "old": "debridr serves a Portuguese page and an English one, with no Portuguese-language commercial content beyond the interface; it is not a Brazilian company as far as the pages read show. It is the only zero-account multi-host found among debrid providers that names 1fichier and Mega together. A 2026-era entrant with localised host pages (pt, ja and others), which is how it surfaced in non-English searches. It states a daily limit exists and never states its size, so it is recorded at the unverified rung rather than estimated. Its 56-host list is broad and current: it includes Fikper-era hosts such as 10drives, Cloudfam and Zincdrive alongside the older Rapidgator/K2S set. The bot is the interesting part: a chat interface removes the need for a browser session and is drivable by a wrapper through the Telegram API. Whether the bot honours the same unstated daily limit was not tested. The host count is settled at 56: the vendors own English page names 56 hosts from Rapidgator to Ubiqfile (read 2026-10-23); the ~70 figure was a lane reading of a different panel and is not a second count. The page was down (HTTP 522) on 2026-11-18, so the 2026-10-23 reading stands.", "new": "\"status\": 523", "rung": "measured", "evidence": {"url": "probe:https://debridr.com/pt", "date": "2026-11-26", "proved": "the probe recorded HTTP 523 verbatim", "capture": "sha256:e8a919a8eb191ccdaa4c6ae340e04cd49d06230ddcc19b3e65697e434fb0d6d0", "quote": "\"status\": 523"}, "added": true, "reason": "the audit found no fresh first-party text; the literal probe status is the only fresh datum"}
